#X text 20 790 The reject outlet is the data: route matches write and load by selector \, so everything to be stored falls out of the reject \, the normal path here., f 44;
#X text 20 990 list append is load-bearing: a message box typed page perform carries page as its selector \, and text set and text search have no method for it (ref/module/state.md)., f 44;
#X text 1620 900 A miss is -1 out of moses' left outlet \, so the t b turns it into text size \, one past the end \, which appends (C-8 \, ref/module/state.md)., f 58;
#X text 1180 1000 Keys match whole atoms \, not prefixes \, so a key may be a prefix of another (ref/module/state.md)., f 44;
#X text 240 1200 Replay resets first \, off the right outlet. An empty or missing file has text size 0 and until runs zero times \, and text get past the end only bangs \, so the loop cannot overrun., f 44;
#X text 1900 460 read -c and write -c must match: without -c on the read \, the file comes back as one line., f 44;
#X text 1180 1330 The path is captured into a symbol object because in a message box \$1 is the incoming message \, not the argument (ref/conventions.md \, C-1)., f 44;
#X obj 900 660 text define \$0-f;
